    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d676">

                <pb facs="0941" n="841" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg841"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.4731/103: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Sydney</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-05-16T19:00:00-04:00">May 16, 1934—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Fundamental issue is diversion of traffic of American origin from American to
                    Canadian railroads and ports, halted in 1929 but resumed when agreement became
                    effective. We gave you language identic with Canadian for purpose of securing
                    privilege identic with that now enjoyed by Canada.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
